// UNSOUNDNESS repro (U1c): an aggregation `for`-variable whose ONLY
// occurrence is in the LEFT operand of a `since`. Range restriction
// propagates only through the since-RIGHT (the anchor; the range-restriction rule —
// the left is a per-step filter, not a range-restrictor), so `w` is not
// range-restricted and the relation does not range over `w`: anchor rows
// carry no `w` column, and the left is evaluated per-step with `w`
// independently re-quantified. Concretely: after a Login anchor, alice reads,
// then bob reads — the true count of users who read at EVERY step is 0, but
// the evaluator counts 1.
//
// Expected: rejected at parse-time binding checks — the `for`-variable `w`
// must be range-restricted by a positive atom in the body.
permit (principal, action == Drupe::Action::"Alert", resource)
when temporal {
    exists (nn: Long). (
        (count for (w: String). where (Drupe::Action::"Read"::request{ input.user: w } since within 1h Drupe::Action::"Login"::request{})) == nn
        && nn >= 1
    )
};
